# Everything here is either rebuilt inside the image, useless to it, or must
# never enter it. Keeping the build context small is also the cheapest speedup
# available: Docker hashes the whole context before it runs the first line.

# Dependencies and build output — reinstalled/rebuilt in the image.
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store
**/dist
**/build
**/.turbo
**/.vite
**/coverage
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets. A .env copied into an image is a secret published to everyone who can
# pull it; .env.example is kept because it is a template with no real values.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# VCS and CI
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Internal planning docs — not part of the distributed boilerplate.
doc

# Editor / OS noise
.idea
.vscode
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log

# Local-only infrastructure and deploy tooling.
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.prod.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
**/Dockerfile
**/.dockerignore
README.md
**/*.md
